CAPVIEW(1)                     User Commands                      CAPVIEW(1)

NAME
    capview - print the capability graph

SYNOPSIS
    capview [PID]

DESCRIPTION
    For every live task, or only for PID, print each occupied capability
    slot: its type, its rights (r w x g m v for read, write, exec, grant,
    mint, revoke), its serial and its parent's serial.

    SERIAL is a capability's identity: 64 bits, issued once and never
    again, so a serial names one capability in one slot. PARENT is the
    serial it was derived from, or "root" for one minted by the kernel.
    The two columns are the nodes and edges of the derivation tree that
    revocation follows (capabilities(7)).

SECURITY
    Needs CAP_DEBUG, which init lends the shell read-only for the
    administrator's session and takes back at logout; in any other session
    the kernel refuses. It observes and changes nothing, and the object
    each capability names is deliberately not reported.

SEE ALSO
    ps(1), capabilities(7)
